From 4e84a32261feb7cacc643fc399de1ccd869425ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:52:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fydroid-rt: add a Game rendering quality slider to
 Display settings

fydroid runs on everything from an RK3588 tablet to a box with a discrete
GPU, so the board's game render target is a starting point rather than an
answer. The slider covers 30%-100% of the panel in the steps AOSP's
app-compat DOWNSCALE changes actually provide, writes the render height
that percentage works out to into Settings.Secure (read by
ArcAppService), and confirms first, because applying one restarts every
running game.

The value line needs its own layout: Settings' seekbar layout has no
@android:id/summary view, so setSummary() is silently dropped.

Localized into the top 10 UI languages (en, zh-CN, zh-TW, ja, ko, es, fr,
de, pt/pt-BR, ru).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I85cbb0ec2ab25260aee16fafab1f2b50c6f08617
---
